thanks to your reporting, that we know

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:53.272
at least some part of the substance

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:54.106
of these documents.

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:54.974
Up till now,

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:55.408
we've seen

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.510
the photographs of the cover sheets.

00:07:57.777 --> 00:07:59.145
There's been a lot made about the fact

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.079
that this is just a cover issue

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:00.646
that was out there.

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.148
It was actually even inside there.

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:03.182
Now we know the substance,

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:04.717
at least in part of one document

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:05.885
and the severity of it.

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:06.919
And no wonder why

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:08.120
there is conversation

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.456
surrounding the unlawful disclosure

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.225
of very secretive information,

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:15.127
the potential diplomatic storm

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:16.028
that could actually result

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:16.796
from all of this.

00:08:16.796 --> 00:08:18.798
And the idea that he was aware of it,

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.900
that he knew the consequences of it

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.168
and was offering to look at it

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:23.970
nonetheless and to undercut somebody

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:25.171
of a high ranking authority

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:26.973
in our own government. Shocking.

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:28.841
So the chairman of the Joint Chiefs,

00:08:28.841 --> 00:08:29.342
General Mark

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:30.843
Milley, is still the chairman

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:32.478
of the Joint Chiefs.

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.113
Do we know if prosecutors have asked him

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:34.680
about this?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.148
Yeah, our reporting team

00:08:36.148 --> 00:08:37.116
with Kaitlan Collins as well.

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:38.618
We were able to confirm

00:08:38.618 --> 00:08:39.685
that General Milley

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:41.787
has been questioned by investigators.

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:44.290
And we also know that the prosecutors

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.592
on this special counsel investigation,

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.427
they also have been asking questions

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:49.529
about Donald Trump's

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:51.163
anger around Mark Milley

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:53.799
and also if there are other circumstances

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:54.667
where he may

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.702
have wanted to show documents

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:58.204
like this or had documents.

00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:00.072
Now, we don't have the answer to

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:02.275
why Donald Trump still had this.

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:04.744
But whenever you look at the course

00:09:04.744 --> 00:09:06.379
of what we are revealing here

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:08.180
and what this investigation is doing,

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.582
one of the things that prosecutors

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:10.816
really need to nail down

00:09:10.816 --> 00:09:12.818
is whether Donald Trump knew

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:14.954
he had this classified document

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:16.822
and if he's talking about Milley

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.524
and he's waving around something

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:19.992
and he's referring to a document

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:21.227
he has from Milley,

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:22.395
that's quite important.

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:24.297
Ellie, if you were on Trump's

00:09:24.297 --> 00:09:25.398
defense team,

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:27.433
how might you defend this recording?

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:29.869
So that's a tough one, Jake.

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:30.503
I think, first of all,

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:31.103
they're going to want

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:32.905
to see the actual transcript

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:33.906
and the recording itself.

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:35.408
They may try to parse the words.

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:37.577
There may be a creative argument

00:09:37.577 --> 00:09:38.311
that, well,

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:38.878
he didn't

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:39.946
legitimately think

00:09:39.946 --> 00:09:41.080
he was doing anything wrong

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.015
because if so, why would he talk about it

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.550
in front of these writers?

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.385
These reporters, I said it's creative.

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:47.954
One thing I do want to stress, though,

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:50.156
one important aspect of Paula and Caitlin

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:51.090
and the team's reporting

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:51.657
is that

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.292
Trump's own team

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:55.394
made these recordings at his request.

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:57.430
There's really sort of shades of Nixon

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:57.697
there.

00:09:57.697 --> 00:09:59.098
And New Jersey is what we call

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:00.833
a one party state, meaning that

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:03.302
as long as one party to the conversation

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:04.804
approved, the recording

00:10:04.804 --> 00:10:05.738
then those recordings

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:06.872
are going to be legal

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:08.641
and potentially admissible against him.

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:10.109
And Laura,

00:10:10.109 --> 00:10:10.977
reading the tea leaves

00:10:10.977 --> 00:10:11.844
of where Jack Smith

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:13.312
is going in his investigation,

00:10:13.312 --> 00:10:14.246
it had seemed as though

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:15.481
he was only

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:17.116
possibly only going to go

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:19.452
after the obstruction of justice charges.

00:10:19.452 --> 00:10:20.853
But this would suggest

00:10:20.853 --> 00:10:24.690
a broader, theoretically broader case.

00:10:24.991 --> 00:10:26.892
Intent is really the final puzzle

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:27.360
for peace.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.294
For any prosecutor,

00:10:28.294 --> 00:10:29.428
it's the hardest thing to prove

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:30.730
because you can't get into the mind

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.131
of the person you're targeting.

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:34.033
But it also makes it a broader case.

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:35.434
You're right away from obstruction.

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:35.801
And now

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:37.570
that the disclosure of information

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.771
also about other

00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:39.972
more expansive

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:40.973
is this document

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:42.742
that was waved around purportedly.

00:10:42.742 --> 00:10:44.010
Do they actually now have it

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.645
or is it a part of another trove

00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:47.013
that is yet to be uncovered?

00:10:47.013 --> 00:10:47.847
It is expanding.

